KG42.register("clusters-b9546b915d8a717a4bc60742",{"id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v142-d-CL003","paper":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization","label":"Contract remuneration after resource activation and the configuration cost interface","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Contract remuneration after resource activation and the configuration cost interface","market_meaning":"After a resource is activated, the SESP manages remuneration according to the respective flexibility contract; CD load, SP load, and generators use their respective billing bases. The configuration chain provides the calculation interface for the corresponding dispatched quantity and contract price, and final payment must still satisfy the actual activation and contract applicability conditions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The interface is limited to the CD, SP, and generator fee line items for the same contract, resource, and time period. The local objects in the configured quantity and payment calculation are retained separately, and planned values do not automatically equal the measured settlement basis; the battery's own operating cost is not included in the external provider's receivable. The SP rate unit and the connection from actual activation to settlement still need to be clarified.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Taking the contractual remuneration obligation of activated resources as an independent outcome, settlement management is associated with its dispatch billing basis. R003 is shared only as an interface, and its optimization decision still belongs to the configuration cluster; the objective function as a whole and the payment line items are not regarded as the same expression, nor are they repeatedly counted as another configuration rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide settlement responsibility, activation trigger conditions, the pay-as-contract principle, and the fee line items for each resource type."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only reference the dispatched quantity, contract price, and the corresponding cost line item in the objective to explain the payment calculation interface; do not again take over the main attribution of the configuration chain, nor treat the plan as verified delivery."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-008","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev02","v141-b-g02-ev05"],"rationale":"The original text explicitly connects the SESP's selection and control of resources with post-activation contractual remuneration, and the fee line items enter the configuration objective. This is a functional and computational interface; it does not add C edges based on narrative order, nor does it equate the overall objective with the individual payment line items."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_delta_start","v141-c-R003::x::var_delta_run","v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_cd"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x001","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x002","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev18","v141-b-g02-ev24"],"rationale":"The disconnection start, continuation state, and contract fee of the same CD resource form an interface for billing by disconnection time period; billing is not calculated by activated energy, and the dispatch state must still satisfy its feasibility conditions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_rho","v141-c-R003::theta::par_v_start","v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_sp"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x003","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta003","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev26","v141-b-g02-ev31","v141-b-g02-ev32","v141-b-g04-e02"],"rationale":"The source text uses the new start time, the baseline start time, and the contract rate together for the SP delay fee. This semantic interface holds, but the difference in rate units between the two chains is not eliminated here, nor is it presumed that every window allows only postponement."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_chi_gr","v141-c-R003::x::var_chi_gd","v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_gr","v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_gd"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x004","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x005","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta004","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev10","v141-b-g02-ev11","v141-b-g02-ev12","v141-b-g04-e02"],"rationale":"For the same type of generator, the curtailed energy in the same time period and the hourly contract price correspond in the configuration cost and the generator payment line item; reducible-output generators and disconnect-only generators are still retained separately."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-015"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the same SESP; unified display does not merge configuration responsibility and settlement responsibility into the same constraint."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_delta_start","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev18","v141-b-g04-e06"],"rationale":"The disconnection start indicator for the same CD load and time period; the roles of configuration decision and billing basis are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_delta_run","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev18","v141-b-g04-e06"],"rationale":"The continuous-disconnection indicator quantity for the same CD load and period; associated with its operation and billing uses, without rewriting the variable."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_rho","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev27","v141-b-g02-ev31","v141-b-g04-e06"],"rationale":"Both are the consumption start period for the same load and moving window, connected to dispatch and delayed billing according to Eq. (16); the variable-domain wording and unit expressions of each are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_chi_gr","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev10","v141-b-g02-ev11","v141-b-g04-e06"],"rationale":"The time-differentiated curtailed energy of the same reducible-output generator, used respectively for configuration and cost calculation; not merged with the interruptible-generator quantity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_chi_gd","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x005"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev10","v141-b-g02-ev11","v141-b-g04-e06"],"rationale":"The time-differentiated curtailed energy of the same interruptible generator, with the same resource category and Eq. (3) semantics; the local uses and original notation of the two chains are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_cd","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g04-e02"],"rationale":"The contractual disconnection fee of the same CD load enters configuration and payment calculation, billed according to the disconnection period; the original NOK unit and notation without a t index are retained, and it is not rewritten as a per-event charge."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM08","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_sp","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev32","v141-b-g02-ev52","v141-b-g04-e02"],"rationale":"Both mean the same SP contract rate, but are recorded respectively as NOK and NOK/period; the appendix and main text also use different unit expressions. As a pending explanatory representational association of the same kind of parameter, do not select a representative or automatically convert."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_v_start","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev26","v141-b-g02-ev32","v141-b-g04-e05"],"rationale":"Both are the baseline consumption start period for the same load and the same moving window; the configuration parameter and the delayed-billing reference are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_gr","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev12","v141-b-g04-e02"],"rationale":"The hourly contract price of the same reducible-output generator, with consistent resource category, period and NOK/kWh unit; the roles in configuration cost and payment calculation are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM11","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_gd","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta005"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev12","v141-b-g04-e02"],"rationale":"The hourly contract price of the same interruptible generator, with consistent resource category, period and NOK/kWh unit; not merged with the rate of the other generator type."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"The contract payment principles and the B entries on which the billing interface depends remain unverified; the quantity correspondence is only a candidate mapping based on the supplied text.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-008","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g02-ev32"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the contract payment conditions, fee subitems and object correspondences; do not treat this assembly as having passed source or scientific independent review."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The SP rate is NOK in R003 and NOK/period in R006; the appendix and case main text also exhibit unit-expression differences. CD fees likewise need to distinguish the price agreement per discrete period from a per-event charge; one cannot infer the charging mode from the symbol omitting the time index.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_sp","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta002","v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_cd","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev06","v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g02-ev32","v141-b-g02-ev52","v141-b-g04-e02"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the conventions for discrete-period counting and price units and the applicable scope of the time resolution, with differences interpreted upstream; do not unify units or perform numerical conversion in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G03","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R006 gives the post-activation remuneration conditions but does not provide a complete Rule-Chain from receiving instructions, device metering, activation termination and delivered quantity to the settlement basis. The source's metering description involves a power difference, whereas the existing generator cost uses an energy quantity; the R003 planned quantity or instantaneous power difference cannot directly replace the final billing energy.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_chi_gr","v141-c-R003::x::var_chi_gd","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-011","v141-b-g02-ev04","v141-b-g02-ev38"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-activated-flexibility-measurement","v141-b-g02-prop04","v141-b-g02-prop03"],"required_work":"The upstream should clarify the relationship among the plan, actual activation and contract settlement, and supplement a sourced metering basis and period linkage; do not fabricate deviation payment or energy integration rules."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G04","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R003's generalization that all costs come from contracts has a scope tension with the battery subsection's ownership and cost-source statement: the battery is owned by SESP, and charging and discharging costs include procurement, network fees, lifetime and opportunity costs. R006 provides no battery payment subitems, so the complete configuration objective cannot be equated with total provider remuneration.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_b_in","v141-c-R003::theta::par_p_b_out","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev05","v141-b-g02-ev16","v141-b-g04-e02"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream should clarify the boundary between the battery's own costs and external contract payments and the applicable scope of the C generalization; if battery settlement rules are needed, evidence should be obtained separately, and the current objects remain frozen."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G05","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The dispatch inputs on which CD and SP billing depend remain affected by gaps in the configuration cluster concerning omission of mutually exclusive states, the time-domain boundary and start-time interpretation. Merely connecting same-named quantities cannot guarantee that the disconnection-period count is valid or that SP fees actually correspond to consumption deferral.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C013","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C014","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C016","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev19","v141-b-g02-ev20","v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g02-ev29","v141-b-g02-ev30","v141-b-g02-ev31"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"After later C versions clarify the CD and SP mathematical conditions listed in the configuration cluster, recheck their fee interfaces; this time do not separately deem the fee subitems a closed final settlement algorithm."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G06","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The contract, contract price and dedicated pay-as-contract proposal still await approval; settlement.payment carries only the existing payment content, and on this basis one must not introduce a uniform clearing price or change contract input prices into clearing results.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-007","v141-b-g01-ev-008","v141-b-g02-ev05","v141-b-g02-ev47","v141-b-g04-e02"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-flexibility-contract","proposal:v141-b-g01-contract-flexibility-price","proposal:v141-b-g01-pay-as-contract-settlement","v141-b-g02-prop02","v141-b-g02-prop05","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Manually evaluate the contract and payment-method proposals, maintaining different rate units and cost attribution; billing interpretations in pending proposals must also be checked and must not be used as approved definitions."}]},"rule_refs":["21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R006","21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-464efdadf92efbd8","COMP-62155e4e7998a74f","COMP-c6ecf48e92525ee2","COMP-f8ab52e76c9b4025"]});
